<title>HUNGARY: Human H1 '97 after-tax profit HUF 497 mln.</title>
<headline>Human H1 '97 after-tax profit HUF 497 mln.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six-month period ending June 30.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of forints unless stated)</p>
<p>				     Jan-June 1997     Jan-June 1996</p>
<p>    Group operating profit	431.6	vs	391.0</p>
<p>    Group pre-tax profit	  497.4	vs	407.4</p>
<p>    Group after-tax profit	497.4	vs	407.4</p>
<p>    Group net sales	     7,943.7	vs    6,544.9</p>
<p>	Domestic sales	    6,731.6	vs    5,948.9</p>
<p>	Export sales		1,212.1	vs	596.0</p>
<p>    Other revenue		    81.6	vs	 42.7</p>
<p>    Direct costs of sales     5,396.5	vs    4,799.3</p>
<p>    Indirect costs of sales   1,896.8	vs    1,222.9</p>
<p>    Other expenditures	    207.8	vs	174.4</p>
<p>    Net financial income	   69.8 profit vs     19.1 profit</p>
<p>	Financial revenue	   130.9	vs	 45.5</p>
<p>	Financial expenditure	61.1	vs	 26.4</p>
<p>    Net extraordinary income	4.0 loss vs	  2.8 loss</p>
<p>	Extraordinary revenue	 0.0	vs	  2.0</p>
<p>	Extraordinary expenditure   4.0	vs	  4.8</p>
<p>    Taxation			    0.0	vs	  0.0</p>
<p>NOTE - Human Oltoanyagtermelo es Gyogyszergyarto Rt is a pharmaceuticals  company. The figures are consolidated, were calculated in accordance  with Hungarian Accounting Standards, and are unaudited.  </p>
<p>Human enjoys a 100 percent tax holiday that it received in 1994 as  its majority shareholder, Canada's Novopharm Ltd, acquired a stake  above 30 percent, the minimum level to qualify for have a tax holiday.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327-4040</p>
</text>
